Execution Plan:\\n## Execution Strategy\\n\\n1.  **Cleanup Phase:** Execute deletion of all existing grid lines and structural columns to clear the workspace for the new 3x3 grid system.\\n2.  **Grid Creation Phase:** Create the new grid lines (G1-G3, H1-H3). This establishes the geometric framework required for column placement.\\n3.  **Structural Column Phase:** Place the 9 structural columns at the defined grid intersections using the pre-existing \'FOUNDATION\' and \'ROOF\' levels as constraints.\\n\\n## Element Creation Order\\n\\n1.  **Delete:** All existing grids (A, B, C, D, E, 07, 06, 05, 04, 03, 02, 01, 1, 2, 3).\\n2.  **Delete:** All existing structural columns of type \'C1\'.\\n3.  **Create Grids:** G1, G2, G3, H1, H2, H3.\\n4.  **Create Columns:** \\n    *   C1 at (G1, H1), (G1, H2), (G1, H3)\\n    *   C1 at (G2, H1), (G2, H2), (G2, H3)\\n    *   C1 at (G3, H1), (G3, H2), (G3, H3)\\n\\n## Naming & Conventions\\n\\n*   **Grid Naming:** Alphanumeric (G1-G3 for vertical, H1-H3 for horizontal).\\n*   **Column Naming:** Type \'C1\'.\\n*   **Conflicts:** The deletion phase is critical. By removing all existing grids and columns first, we eliminate potential naming collisions with the new grid/column set.\\n*   **Uniqueness:** Ensure no duplicate grid names are generated during the batch process.\\n\\n## Revit Constraints\\n\\n*   **Level Dependency:** The \'FOUNDATION\' and \'ROOF\' levels are pre-existing and must be referenced by their internal Revit IDs.\\n*   **Grid Extents:** The design manual specifies a 40 ft extent for a 40 ft footprint. To prevent Revit visibility clipping, the orchestrator should ensure the grid line extents are set to at least 45 ft (exceeding the outermost column coordinate of 20 ft).\\n*   **Coordinate Origin:** All placements are relative to (0,0,0) at the intersection of G2 and H2.\\n*   **Pre-existing Elements:** Levels are marked as PRE-EXISTING; the parser must NOT attempt to create these.\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n\\nTh