 of the grid system (Intersection of G2 and H2).\\n*   **Units:** Feet (ft).\\n\\n## 2. Levels\\n| Name | Elevation (ft) | Status | Notes |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| FOUNDATION | -3.773 | PRE-EXISTING | Base Level for Columns |\\n| GROUND FLOOR | 1.148 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n| FIRST FLOOR | 12.139 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n| ROOF | 23.13 | PRE-EXISTING | Top Level for Columns |\\n| PARAPET | 31.332 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n| Level 1 | 0.0 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n| Level 2 | 12.0 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n| Test Level 99 | 99.0 | PRE-EXISTING | |\\n\\n## 3. Grid Lines\\n| Name | Direction | Offset from Origin (ft) | Extent (ft) | Status |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| G1 | Vertical (Y) | -20 | 40 | NEW |\\n| G2 | Vertical (Y) | 0 | 40 | NEW |\\n| G3 | Vertical (Y) | 20 | 40 | NEW |\\n| H1 | Horizontal (X) | -20 | 40 | NEW |\\n| H2 | Horizontal (X) | 0 | 40 | NEW |\\n| H3 | Horizontal (X) | 20 | 40 | NEW |\\n\\n## 4. Structural Columns\\n| Grid Intersection | X (ft) | Y (ft) | Base Level | Top Level | Base Offset (ft) | Top Offset (ft) | Rotation (\\u00b0) | Family/Type |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| G1-H1 | -20 | -20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G1-H2 | -20 | 0 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G1-H3 | -20 | 20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G2-H1 | 0 | -20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G2-H2 | 0 | 0 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G2-H3 | 0 | 20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G3-H1 | 20 | -20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G3-H2 | 20 | 0 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n| G3-H3 | 20 | 20 | FOUNDATION | ROOF | 0 | 0 | 0 | C1 |\\n\\n## 5. Deletion Instructions\\n*   **Grids:** Delete all existing grids (A, B, C, D, E, 07, 06, 05, 04, 03, 02, 01, 1, 2, 3).\\n*   **Columns:** Delete all 21 existing structural columns of type \'C1\'.", "[BIM Execution Planner] Phase 3 \\u2014 Formulating execution strategy...", "[BIM Execution Planner] Execution Plan:\\n## Execution Strategy\\n\\n1.  **Cleanup Phase:** Execute deletion of all existing grid lines and structural columns to clear the workspace for the new 3x3 grid system.\\n2.  **Grid Creation Phase:** Create the new grid lines (G1-G3, H1-H3). This establishes the geometric framework required for column placement.\\n3.  **Structural Column Phase:** Place the 9 structural columns at the defined grid intersections using the pre-existing \'FOUNDATION\' and \'ROOF\' levels as constraints.\\n\\n## Element Creation Order\\n\\n1.  **Delete:** All existing grids (A, B, C, D, E, 07, 06, 05, 04, 03, 02, 01, 1, 2, 3).\\n2.  **Delete:** All existing structural columns of type \'C1\'.\\n3.  **Create Grids:** G1, G2, G3, H1, H2, H3.\\n4.  **Create Columns:** \\n    *   C1 at (G1, H1), (G1, H2), (G1, H3)\\n    *   C1 at (G2, H1), (G2, H2), (G2, H3)\\n    *   C1 at (G3, H1), (G3, H2), (G3, H3)\\n\\n## Naming & Conventions\\n\\n*   **Grid Naming:** Alphanumeric (G1-G3 for vertical, H1-H3 for horizontal).\\n*   **Column Naming:** Type \'C1\'.\\n*   **Conflicts:** The deletion phase is critical. By removing all existing grids and columns first, we eliminate potential naming collisions with the new grid/column set.\\n*   **Uniqueness:** Ensure no duplicate grid names are generated during the batch process.\\n\\n## Revit Constraints\\n\\n*   **Level Dependency:** The \'FOUNDATION\' and \'ROOF\' levels are pre-existing and must be referenced by their internal Revit IDs.\\n*   **Grid Extents:** The design manual specifies a 40 ft extent for a 40 ft footprint. To prevent Revit visibility clipping, the orchestrator should ensure the grid line extents are set to at least 45 ft (exceeding the outermost column coordinate of 20 ft).\\n*   **Coordinate Origin:** All placements are relative to (0,0,0) at the intersection of G2 and H2.\\n*   **Pre-existing Elements:** Levels are marked as PRE-EXISTING; the parser must NOT attempt to create these.\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n\\nThe `BIMValidatorAgent` must verify the following post-execution:\\n\\n1.  **Grid Spacing:** Verify that the distance between G1-G2, G2-G3, H1-H2, and H2-H3 is exactly 20 ft.\\n2.  **Level Assignment:** Confirm all 9 columns have `base_level_id` mapped to \'FOUNDATION\' (-3.773 ft) and `top_level_id` mapped to \'ROOF\' (23.13 ft).\\n3.  **Column Coordinates:** Verify that the center point of each column matches the intersection coordinates:\\n    *   (-20, -20), (-20, 0), (-20, 20)\\n    *   (0, -20), (0, 0), (0, 20)\\n    *   (20, -20), (20, 0), (20, 20)\\n4.  **Cleanup Verification:** Confirm that the count of grids is exactly 6 and the count of columns is exactly 9.", "[BIM Parser] Phase 4 \\u2014 Translating Input Design Manual to tool-call JSON...", "[BIM Parser] Batch payload ready \\u2014 15 tool call(s) to execute.", "[BIM Orchestrator] Phase 5 \\u2014 Dispatching batch transaction to Revit...", "[BIM Parser] Phase 6 \\u2014 Reverse-parsing execution results to Result Design Manual...", "[BIM Parser] Result Design Manual:\\n\\n# Result Design Manual\\n\\n## Summary\\nTotal calls dispatched | Succeeded | Failed\\n--- | --- | ---\\n15 | 15 | 0\\n\\n## Created Levels\\n| Name | Elevation (ft) | Element ID | Status |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| N/A | N/A | N/A | No levels were created in this batch. |\\n\\n## Created Grids\\n| Name | start_x | start_y | end_x | end_y | Element ID | Status |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| G1 | -20.0 | -22.5 | -20.0 | 22.5 | 11446f6f-d425-49d2-8843-6abbf7d80efd-001360aa | Success |\\n| G2 | 0.0 | -22.5 | 0.0 | 22.5 | 11446f6f-d425-49d2-8843-6abbf7d80efd-001360ab | Success |\\n| G3 | 20.0 | -22.5 | 20.0 | 22.5 | 11446f6f-d425-49d2-8843-6abbf7d80efd-001360ac | Success |\\n| H1 | -22.5 | -20.0 | 22.5 | -20.0 | 11446f6f-d425-49d2-8843-6abbf7d80efd-001360ad | Success |\\n| H2 | -22.5 | 0.0 | 22.5 | 0.0 | 11446f6f-d425-49d2-8843-6abbf7d80efd-001360ae | Success |\\n| H3 | -22.5 | 20.0 | 22.5 | 20.0 | 11446f6f-d425-49