Analysing design requirements...", "[BIM Design Manual] Phase 2 \\u2014 Generating complete numeric Input Design Manual...", "[BIM Design Manual] Input Design Manual compiled:\\n\\n# BIM Design Manual: 3x3 Grid and Structural Layout\\n\\nThis manual specifies the cleanup of existing project elements and the creation of a new 3x3 structural grid system. All units are in feet.\\n\\n## Levels\\n| Name | Elevation | Status |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| GROUND FLOOR | 1.148 | PRE-EXISTING |\\n| FIRST FLOOR | 12.139 | PRE-EXISTING |\\n| FOUNDATION | -3.773 | TO_DELETE |\\n| ROOF | 23.13 | TO_DELETE |\\n| PARAPET | 31.332 | TO_DELETE |\\n| Level 1 | 0.0 | TO_DELETE |\\n| Level 2 | 12.0 | TO_DELETE |\\n| Test Level 99 | 99.0 | TO_DELETE |\\n\\n## Grid Lines\\nGrid lines are spaced at 20ft intervals. Vertical grids (1, 2, 3) span Y= -5 to 45. Horizontal grids (A, B, C) span X= -5 to 45.\\n\\n| Name | Start X | Start Y | End X | End Y | Status |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| 1 | 0.0 | -5.0 | 0.0 | 45.0 | NEW |\\n| 2 | 20.0 | -5.0 | 20.0 | 45.0 | NEW |\\n| 3 | 40.0 | -5.0 | 40.0 | 45.0 | NEW |\\n| A | -5.0 | 0.0 | 45.0 | 0.0 | NEW |\\n| B | -5.0 | 20.0 | 45.0 | 20.0 | NEW |\\n| C | -5.0 | 40.0 | 45.0 | 40.0 | NEW |\\n| A, B, C, D, E, 07, 06, 05, 04, 03, 02, 01, 1, 2, 3, G1, G2, G3, H1, H2, H3 | N/A | N/A | N/A | N/A | TO_DELETE |\\n\\n## Structural Columns\\nAll existing columns (30 total) are to be deleted. New columns are placed at the 9 grid intersections.\\n\\n| X | Y | Base Level | Top Level | Status |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| 0.0 | 0.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 20.0 | 0.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 40.0 | 0.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 0.0 | 20.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 20.0 | 20.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 40.0 | 20.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 0.0 | 40.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 20.0 | 40.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| 40.0 | 40.0 | GROUND FLOOR | FIRST FLOOR | NEW |\\n| All Existing | N/A | N/A | N/A | TO_DELETE |\\n\\n## Diagnostic Report\\n*   **Status:** Ready for execution.\\n*   **Missing Context:** The `UniqueId`s for the existing 30 structural columns and 21 grid lines must be retrieved via `fetch_structural_columns` and `fetch_grids` prior to the `execute_batch` call.\\n*   **Resolution:** The Parser agent must perform the fetch operations first, map the returned IDs to the `TO_DELETE` status items above, and then construct the `execute_batch` payload.", "[BIM Execution Planner] Phase 3 \\u2014 Formulating execution strategy...", "[BIM Execution Planner] Execution Plan:\\n## Execution Strategy\\n\\n1.  **Cleanup Phase:** Execute deletion of all redundant levels, grid lines, and structural columns to clear the workspace and prevent naming collisions.\\n2.  **Datum Verification:** Confirm the existence and elevation of the required base levels (GROUND FLOOR and FIRST FLOOR).\\n3.  **Reference Layout:** Generate the new 3x3 grid system (Grids 1-3 and A-C) with the specified 20ft spacing.\\n4.  **Structural Host Placement:** Instantiate the 9 structural columns at the defined grid intersections, constrained to the verified levels.\\n5.  **Validation:** Perform a final audit of element counts and geometric constraints.\\n\\n## Element Creation Order\\n\\n1.  **Deletion (Cleanup):**\\n    *   Delete all 30 existing structural columns.\\n    *   Delete all 21 existing grid lines (A, B, C, D, E, 07, 06, 05, 04, 03, 02, 01, 1, 2, 3, G1, G2, G3, H1, H2, H3).\\n    *   Delete redundant levels: FOUNDATION, ROOF, PARAPET, Level 1, Level 2, Test Level 99.\\n2.  **Reference Layer (Grids):**\\n    *   Create Grid 1 (0, -5 to 0, 45)\\n    *   Create Grid 2 (20, -5 to 20, 45)\\n    *   Create Grid 3 (40, -5 to 40, 45)\\n    *   Create Grid A (-5, 0 to 45, 0)\\n    *   Create Grid B (-5, 20 to 45, 20)\\n    *   Create Grid C (-5, 40 to 45, 40)\\n3.  **Host Layer (Columns):**\\n    *   Create 9 Structural Columns at intersections: (0,0), (20,0), (40,0), (0,20), (20,20), (40,20), (0,40), (20,40), (40,40).\\n    *   Set Base Level: GROUND FLOOR, Top Level: FIRST FLOOR for all.\\n\\n## Naming & Conventions\\n\\n*   **Grids:** Numeric labels (1, 2, 3) for vertical lines; Alpha labels (A, B, C) for horizontal lines.\\n*   **Levels:** Retain existing names \\"GROUND FLOOR\\" and \\"FIRST FLOOR\\".\\n*   **Conflicts:** The deletion of all existing grids and columns is mandatory before creating new ones to avoid \\"Duplicate Name\\" errors or overlapping geometry.\\n\\n## Revit Constraints\\n\\n*   **Grid Extents:** Grids are defined from -5.0 to 45.0 to ensure they extend 5ft beyond the outermost columns (located at 0.0 and 40.0), preventing visibility clipping in plan views.\\n*   **Host Validity:** Columns must be hosted on \\"GROUND FLOOR\\" and constrained to \\"FIRST FLOOR\\".\\n*   **Transaction Integrity:** All operations must be wrapped in a single `execute_batch` transaction to ensure that if any deletion or creation fails, the model state remains consistent.\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n\\n*   **Grid Count:** Verify exactly 6 grid lines exist.\\n*   **Column Count:** Verify exactly 9 structural columns exist.\\n*   **Level Check:** Verify \\"GROUND FLOOR\\" (1.148) and \\"FIRST FLOOR\\" (12.139) are the only remaining levels.\\n*   **Geometric Check:** Ensure all columns are placed at the exact coordinates (0,0), (20,0), (40,0), (0,20), (20,20), (40,20), (0,40), (20,40), (40,40).\\n*   **Constraint Check:** Confirm all columns have `Base Level` = GROUND FLOOR and `Top Level` = FIRST FLOOR.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Diagnostic Report\\n*   **Status:** Ready for execution.\\n*   **Pre-requisite:** The Parser must call `fetch_structural_columns` and `fetch_grids` to obtain the `UniqueId`s for the 30 columns and 21 grids identified for deletion.\\n*   **Resolution:** Map the fetched IDs to the `delete_structural_column` and `delete_grid` tool calls within 