 Create the new grid system (X1-X3, Y1-Y3) to establish the structural coordinate system.\\n3. **Host Phase**: Place structural columns (C1) at the defined intersections of the new grid lines, constrained between the FOUNDATION and ROOF levels.\\n\\n## Element Creation Order\\n1. **Deletion (Cleanup)**:\\n   - `delete_structural_column` (13 instances)\\n   - `delete_grid` (12 instances)\\n2. **Reference Layer**:\\n   - `create_grid` (X1, X2, X3, Y1, Y2, Y3)\\n3. **Host Layer**:\\n   - `create_structural_column` (9 instances at coordinates: (0,0), (0,20), (0,40), (20,0), (20,20), (20,40), (40,0), (40,20), (40,40))\\n\\n## Naming & Conventions\\n- **Grids**: Labeled X1, X2, X3 (vertical) and Y1, Y2, Y3 (horizontal).\\n- **Columns**: Type \'C1\' used for all structural columns.\\n- **Levels**: Existing levels \'FOUNDATION\' and \'ROOF\' are used as the base and top constraints respectively.\\n- **Conflicts**: All existing grids and columns are being purged to prevent naming or ID collisions with the new layout.\\n\\n## Revit Constraints\\n- **Grid Extents**: Grids are defined from 0 to 40 feet in both X and Y directions, ensuring they fully encompass the 40x40 footprint of the column layout to prevent visibility clipping.\\n- **Host Validity**: Columns must be hosted on the \'FOUNDATION\' level. The \'ROOF\' level is used as the top constraint.\\n- **Coordinate System**: The origin (0,0) is anchored at the intersection of Grid X1 and Y1.\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n- **Grid Count**: Verify exactly 6 grid lines exist in the project.\\n- **Column Count**: Verify exactly 9 structural columns exist.\\n- **Grid Geometry**: Confirm grid endpoints match the specified (0,0) to (40,40) range.\\n- **Column Constraints**: \\n    - Verify all 9 columns have `base_level_id` = \'FOUNDATION\'.\\n    - Verify all 9 columns have `top_level_id` = \'ROOF\'.\\n- **Type Check**: Confirm all columns are of type \'C1\'.", "[BIM Parser] Phase 4 \\u2014 Translating Input Design Manual to too